<title>INDIA: Indian Shipping -- Mangalore cargoes - Nov 14.</title>
<headline>Indian Shipping -- Mangalore cargoes - Nov 14.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is the berthing schedule of major vessels loading and unloading at India's Mangalore port on November 14:</p>
<p>  Commodity	     Tons		   Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>		    (LDD/ULD) (Balance)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Scrap		   875 (ULD) 15,547    Beta Luck	  7/11</p>
<p> Timber		2,413 (ULD)  1,940    Wood Pecker     10/11</p>
<p> Urea		  1,013 (ULD)    774    Sai Kung	   1/11</p>
<p> Timber		  321 (ULD)    816    Irufa	     12/11</p>
<p> Muriate Of Potash   982 (ULD)  1,284    Hun Jian	   1/11</p>
<p> LPG		   3,500 (ULD)    ---    Gaj Mazor	 13/11</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Note:</p>
<p>ULD-Discharge</p>
<p>LDD-Loading</p>
<p>(Source: J.M.Baxi &amp; Co, Mangalore)</p>
<p>Lloyds Shipping adds:</p>
<p>Mangalore - 19 vessels due, 2-3 days delay expected, 1 vessel loading at berth, 3 discharging at berth, 1 awaiting berth, 1 other.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
